SUMMARY:National Day of Remembrance and Action on Violence Against Women
DESCRIPTION:December 6 is the National Day of Remembrance and Action on Violence Against Women. \nJoin the U of T Engineering community on Monday\, December 7\, 2026 at 6pm on the steps of the Galbraith Building for a student-led ceremony to honour the lives of the 14 women killed at Montreal’s École Polytechnique in 1989. \nTo mark the 37th anniversary of this devastating act of misogyny\, we will join together in collective grief for all those lost to gender-based violence as we remember those who were killed\, and look toward a better future. \nAll are welcome to join. Learn more about the National Day of Remember and Action on Violence Against Women \n— \nWant to get involved? Build days and ceremony planning takes place on November 21\, 22\, 28\, 29 and Dec 5 in the Myhal Centre’s EngSoc Arena. Drop in any time to help build this year’s display (no experience required).\n \n 
URL:https://www.engineering.utoronto.ca/event/national-day-of-remembrance-and-action-on-violence-against-women-7/
LOCATION:Galbraith Building\, 35 St George St\, Toronto\, Ontario\, M5S 1A4\, Canada
END:VEVENT
